    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "MusicEvent",
      "id": "8cacd4cb8c20d4b0",
      "title": "EDEN presents Daria Kolosova b2b HECTOR OAKS",
      "description": "",
      "fullDescription": "The columns of the Athens Conservatoire have witnessed music education for generations. Tonight they witness something else — Daria Kolosova and Hector Oaks meeting behind the decks for a back-to-back that refuses to behave.\n\nEDEN brings this pairing to the Conservatoire as statement: techno belongs everywhere music is taken seriously. Kolosova's Ukrainian intensity — sets that build through relentless accumulation — meets Oaks' Spanish-via-Berlin weight, his reputation for hardware-driven productions that sound like machines arguing with each other. When they go B2B, the exchange becomes the art.\n\nThe Athens Conservatoire provides the unlikely setting that makes this evening essential. This is where Athens trains its classical musicians, where tradition matters, where the architecture itself suggests restraint. Tonight's programming inverts all of that — the institution becomes the rave, the concert hall becomes the dance floor, the marble and wood absorb frequencies they never anticipated.\n\nThe crowd navigates the contradiction with relish. These are techno heads who understand the joke and the point: that electronic music deserves the same spaces classical music occupies, that the Conservatoire's acoustic precision serves techno as well as it serves Brahms. Students and professionals, locals and visitors, everyone amused and elevated by the setting.\n\nIf you want the usual warehouse, if the venue should disappear behind the music, EDEN at the Conservatoire operates on different logic. The setting is part of the experience — dancing where your grandmother heard her first recital, sweating where serious people have serious music thoughts. But if you've been searching for techno that claims cultural space, that insists electronic music belongs in high rooms — tonight, the Conservatoire learns what its acoustics were really built for.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Sunday, February 22, 2026 |\n| **Venue** | Athens Conservatoire |\n| **Getting there** | Central Athens location |\n| **Price** | Check EDEN announcements |\n\nThe Conservatoire thought it was just teaching music. Tonight it becomes the lesson.",
      "startDate": "2026-02-22T17:30:00",
      "endDate": null,
      "type": "opera",
      "genres": [
        "electronic"
      ],
      "tags": [],
