    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "MusicEvent",
      "id": "9ba58276727ac49b",
      "title": "EDEN presents DARIA KOLOSOVA b2b HECTOR OAKS",
      "description": "22 Φεβρουαριου EDEN presents DARIA KOLOSOVA b2b HECTOR OAKS Athens Conservatoire (in Greek)",
      "fullDescription": "The concert hall was built for classical music. Tonight it will discover what happens when Ukrainian techno precision meets Spanish-Berlin industrial weight, and neither artist has any interest in being polite about it.\n\nDaria Kolosova has built her reputation on sets that refuse release. She accumulates intensity through layered percussion, hypnotic repetition, the relentless forward motion that defines Ukrainian techno's contribution to the European scene. Hector Oaks matches that intensity with different tools — his productions favor the hardware growl, sounds that feel machined rather than programmed. When they meet for back-to-back sets, the negotiation becomes the performance.\n\nEDEN has secured the Athens Conservatoire for this encounter, and the setting sharpens everything. The venue has trained musicians since the 19th century; its halls carry the weight of tradition. Tonight that tradition absorbs frequencies its architects never anticipated, and the contrast makes the music hit differently. Dancing where classical musicians practiced scales — the irony operates on everyone present.\n\nThe crowd comes prepared for the collision. These are techno heads who track EDEN announcements, who recognize both names and understand what the B2B format promises. The Conservatoire's unfamiliar setting adds a layer — people genuinely curious whether the architecture can handle what's coming. (It can. The acoustics were built for sound, after all.)\n\nIf you need your techno in industrial spaces, if the venue should match the music's rawness, tonight inverts those expectations. The formality becomes fuel. But if you've been searching for the night that proves electronic music belongs in every room that's ever hosted serious music — the Conservatoire tonight learns new lessons from its students.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Sunday, February 22, 2026 |\n| **Venue** | The Conservatoire (Odeio Athinon) |\n| **Getting there** | Central Athens location |\n| **Price** | Check EDEN announcements |\n\nDaria Kolosova. Hector Oaks. The Conservatoire. Read those names again.",
