    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "MusicEvent",
      "id": "7954e19a7e7569ae",
      "title": "Doros Dimosthenous sings Elvis - \"Carnival with… the King\"",
      "description": "",
      "fullDescription": "The sideburns catch the light before you hear the first note. Then the band kicks in and Memphis arrives in Mets, filtered through an Athenian voice that's spent years learning how the King made sound become feeling.\n\nDoros Dimosthenous returns to Half Note for the second night of his Elvis tribute, and the word \"tribute\" barely covers it. This is inhabited performance — the gestures, the timing, the vocal catches that made Presley's catalog survive decades of imitation. Dimosthenous doesn't impersonate so much as channel, and the difference matters when the songs are ones you thought you knew completely.\n\nHalf Note Jazz Club offers the setting these ballads deserve. The Mets institution has hosted jazz royalty since 1979, and tonight it bends its programming toward rock and roll royalty of a different kind. The room holds maybe 200 people, close enough to catch the performer's expression, intimate enough that \"Love Me Tender\" actually feels tender rather than theatrical.\n\nThe Sunday night crowd differs subtly from Saturday's. Some are returners — people who came last night and couldn't stay away. Others are the ones who needed to hear how the first night went before committing. The result is a room even more prepared for what Dimosthenous delivers, permission for transport already granted before he takes the stage.\n\nIf you're a purist who believes no one should touch the King's catalog, if tribute feels inherently lesser, this evening asks you to reconsider. Dimosthenous proves that devotion can be creative, that interpretation honors rather than diminishes. But if you've been ready for an evening where Elvis's songs meet Half Note's acoustic intimacy, where the love songs land the way they're meant to — tonight, the King's spirit visits Mets again.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Sunday, February 22, 2026 |\n| **Venue** | Half Note Jazz Club |\n| **Address** | Trivonianou 17, Mets |\n| **Getting there** | Akropoli Metro (Red line), 10-minute walk |\n| **Price** | Table: 15-20 euro, Bar: 10-15 euro |\n| **Reservations** | Essential - book ahead |\n\nSame voice, same venue, different night. The songs remain immortal.",
      "startDate": "2026-02-22T21:30:00",
      "endDate": null,
      "type": "concert",
      "genres": [
        "jazz"
      ],
